      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "McDonald Property, Lucan's longest-established estate agents, are delighted to present No. 64 Arthur Griffith Park to the market. This bright, very well maintained three-bedroom mid-terrace family home is perfectly positioned in a peaceful cul-de-sac, offering a safe, traffic-free environment and a sense of privacy.\n\nA standout feature of this property is its impressive B-energy rating, making it highly energy-efficient and eligible for green mortgage rates.\n\nAccommodation Overview\nThe ground floor has an entrance porch leading into a hallway. To the front, a living room features wood-effect laminate flooring and large windows that fill the space with natural light. To the rear, a separate, modern kitchen comes fully equipped with cream coloured kitchen units, tiled splashback, quality appliances, and direct access to the private garden.\n\nUpstairs, the property features three well-proportioned bedrooms, each finished with clean laminate flooring.\n\nA family bathroom completes the accommodation, featuring tiled flooring and a reliable Triton T90 electric shower.\n\nGarden Exterior\nThe front offers a walled garden with a private driveway for convenient off-street parking, alongside abundant communal parking nearby.\n\nThe large, private rear garden is fully walled and laid out with a blend of paving and lawnperfect for outdoor dining and play.\n\nAt the end of the garden sits a solid, block-built outhouse, offering versatility to be transformed into a home office, gym, or playroom.\n\n \n\nLOCATION: \n\nSituated in a most convenient Lucan location, the property is just a three-minute stroll from local schools, expansive amenity greens, frequent bus routes, and the SuperValu Shopping Centre, which houses a library, medical centre, and local cafs.\n\n \n\nKEY FEATURES\n\nEnergy Efficient (BER B): ensures lower utility bills and eligibility for lower-interest Green Mortgages.\n\nChain-Free Sale: Ready for immediate occupancy, ensuring a smoother, faster transaction.\n\nQuiet Cul-de-Sac: Excellent privacy with no passing traffic and generous additional parking.\n\nVersatile Outhouse: Solid block-built structure at the rear, ideal for a home office, studio, or playroom.\n\nTurn-Key Appeal: Double-glazed windows, reliable gas fired central heating, and bright interiors maximizing natural light.\n\nConvenience: Just minutes on foot from schools, transport links, and local shopping facilities.\n\nACCOMMODATION DETAILS:\n\nGround Floor:\n\nEntrance Porch: Tiled flooring.\n\nEntrance Hallway: Carpeted flooring with practical under-stairs storage.\n\nLiving Room: Positioned to the front with wood-effect laminate flooring and fitted blinds.\n\nKitchen: Located to the rear with cream-colored eye and floor-level units, white tiled splashback, Hotpoint washing machine, Vaillant gas boiler, and access to the rear garden.\n\nFirst Floor:\n\nMaster Bedroom: Spacious double room to the front with laminate flooring and fitted blinds.\n\nBedroom 2: Bright double room to the rear with laminate flooring and fitted blinds.\n\nBedroom 3: Cozy single room to the front with laminate flooring and built-in wardrobe/shelving.Family\n\nBathroom: Tiled flooring, partially tiled walls, WC, WHB, bath, and a Triton T90 electric shower.\n\n \n\nMeasurements provided are approximate and intended for guidance. Descriptions, photographs and floor plans are provided for illustrative and guidance purposes. Errors, omissions, inaccuracies, or mis-descriptions in these materials do not entitle any party to claims, actions, or compensation against McDonald Property or the vendor. Prospective buyers or interested parties are responsible for conducting their own due diligence, inspections, or other inquiries to verify the accuracy of the information provided. McDonald Property have not tested any appliances, apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Prospective buyers or interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items"
